  "default_status": "no_verified_installer",
  "notes": [
    "Windows NVIDIA 24 GB+ Automatic/LiteRT uses the LiteRT 26B route only after physical 24 GB+ NVIDIA validation; until then it remains pending_validation.",
    "Windows NVIDIA below 24 GB, AMD, and CPU-only selections with Runtime=LiteRT are unsupported by the live checker and should be redirected to Ollama rather than treated as missing installer work.",
    "Windows CPU-only 8 GB Automatic/Ollama is tracked as pending validation, not released.",
    "Windows CPU-only 16–31 GB routes to E4B QAT; 32 GB+ routes to 12B QAT.",
    "Windows AMD Automatic and Windows NVIDIA Automatic below 24 GB route to the verified Ollama E2B package.",
    "Released routing rules only point to verified profiles.",
    "macOS Apple Silicon Automatic uses LiteRT at 24 GB+ unified memory and Ollama below 24 GB, matching the live checker; packages are not released yet.",
    "Linux NVIDIA Automatic uses LiteRT at 24 GB+ VRAM and Ollama below 24 GB; Linux AMD and CPU-only use Ollama. Cross-platform packages remain pending product definition.",
    "Explicit LiteRT selections that the live checker rejects are classified unsupported_route instead of being counted as missing installer work."
  ]
